# Negative steering, three stages, 6R8M (engineered Pikp1-HMA NK-KE / AVR-PikE).
# Sourced from the n=50 dose sweep, the run the thesis figures report.
#
#   #1  solved complex          cold start 35.98 A -> steered 2.44 A
#   #2  cold-start prediction   the effector on the wrong face (seed 0)
#   #3  steered prediction      design_37, seed 2, 6 mutations, 3/3 seeds
#
# Everything is superposed on the SOLVED HMA, so the three effector positions
# are directly comparable. Only the solved HMA is drawn; the cold-start and
# steered HMAs are hidden, because all three are the same fold and drawing
# them would just thicken the receptor without adding information.
#
# The steering mutations are shown on the solved HMA in red. Their positions
# come from the engine as prediction numbering (/A:20,22,23,26,27,59) and are
# mapped here to the solved structure's numbering, which starts at 184. The
# offset is +185 and every wild-type residue was checked to match:
#   K20D -> 205   M22R -> 207   A23K -> 208
#   A26K -> 211   S27R -> 212   A59R -> 244
#
# The camera matrix reproduces the orientation of the original interactive
# renders. It is set once with all three models shown, so every panel shares
# one camera and the panels stay comparable.

# Paths are relative to the repo root, so run ChimeraX from there:
#
#   chimerax --script analysis/01-pose-rescue/negsteer_stages_6R8M.cxc
#
# The two prediction paths are under experiments/, which is gitignored, so
# they need the n50 dose-sweep run tree present. contrib/sync_from_hpc.sh
# --name dose-sweep pulls it.

close session

open data/reference_complexes/6R8M.pdb
open experiments/dose-sweep/n50/6R8M/run/cycle_0/initial_prediction.pdb
open experiments/dose-sweep/n50/6R8M/run/cycle_0/steered/design_37_s2/prediction.pdb

rename #1 solved
rename #2 coldstart
rename #3 steered

matchmaker #2/A to #1/A
matchmaker #3/A to #1/A

hide atoms
show cartoon

hide #2/A cartoon
hide #3/A cartoon

color #1/A cornflowerblue
color #1/B lightgreen
color #2/B gray
color #3/B green

set bgColor white
lighting flat
graphics silhouettes true

view matrix camera -0.336034,-0.422125,0.841957,230.018677,0.491680,-0.841084,-0.225453,-69.833373,0.803326,0.338214,0.490183,146.638901
view
zoom 1.85

# Panel 1, the solved complex on its own.
hide #2 models
hide #3 models
save analysis/01-pose-rescue/raw-images/6R8M_solved.png width 3000 height 3000 supersample 3

# Panel 2, add the cold-start effector.
show #2 models
hide #2/A cartoon
save analysis/01-pose-rescue/raw-images/6R8M_coldstart.png width 3000 height 3000 supersample 3

# Panel 3, add the steered effector and mark the steering mutations.
show #3 models
hide #3/A cartoon
color #1/A:205,207,208,211,212,244 red
show #1/A:205,207,208,211,212,244 atoms
style #1/A:205,207,208,211,212,244 stick
hide #1/A:205,207,208,211,212,244@N,C,O,H* atoms
save analysis/01-pose-rescue/raw-images/6R8M_steered.png width 3000 height 3000 supersample 3

exit
